# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SuperCitycon — what does NOT belong in the repository
#
# The rule: ONE copy of the game. Every model binary is committed exactly
# once (in game/public/assets/models). Everything below is either derived
# from that, or source material that already lives elsewhere.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Dependencies — reinstalled by `npm ci`. (The bare name also catches the
# convenience symlink at the workspace root.)
node_modules
node_modules/

# The build output. `npm run build` regenerates it in about ten seconds, and
# committing it would put a SECOND copy of every model binary in the history.
game/dist/

# The release package. It is a build artefact, rebuilt byte-for-byte by
# `node tools/package-release.mjs`, and it deliberately contains the built
# bundle — so committing it would put a THIRD copy of every model binary in
# the history. The package lives on disk at `release/`; the recipe for
# rebuilding it is in `docs/release/RELEASE-MANIFEST.md`.
#
# Root-anchored on purpose: a bare `release/` also matches `docs/release/`,
# which would silently drop the six release documents from version control.
# They ARE release content and must be committed.
/release/

# The raw library archives and their extracted trees. They are source
# material for the asset curator and live in ~/.minimax/asset-library.
# The KayKit City Builder pack is the exception: it exists nowhere else, so
# it travels with the game.
game/public/assets/extracted/
game/public/assets/*.zip
!game/public/assets/kaykit-city-builder.zip

# Scratch
.DS_Store
*.log
Thumbs.db

# Tool runtime state, not project content.
.serena/

# The 3D design package's downloaded asset archives (2.4 GB, 23 zips).
#
# These are NOT project content. They are a cache of archives that already
# exist in the public upstream repository, re-fetchable with
# `minimax-game/tools/fetch-3d-packs.sh` and `fetch-remaining-3d.sh`.
#
# They ARE required to re-verify the design's 849 cited asset paths: the
# gate resolves each cited path against the real archive listings, and with
# the cache removed 721 of the 849 fail to resolve. The path INVENTORY in
# `minimax-game/platformer-docs/library-inventory/` (10 MB) is what travels
# with the repository; the archives stay on the machine that fetched them.
minimax-game/platformer-docs/library-packs/

# Python bytecode cache from the design gates.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# A tool's ad-hoc output. `tools/profile-city.mjs --outdir verification/…`
# writes there by default during a manual run; the report belongs in the
# evidence directory, not in the repository.
verification/
